      "pr_number": 26419,
      "sha": "fea4498ea5e7ba7687aab2619417eed9139960eb",
      "base_sha": "",
      "subject": "Fix #26401: EXISTS returns false when its subquery filters on an aggregate over an empty table",
      "body": "Fixes #26401.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`EXISTS` returns false (and `NOT EXISTS` returns rows) when its subquery filters on an aggregate over an empty table:\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nCREATE TABLE t (a INT);\r\nINSERT INTO t VALUES (1), (2);\r\nCREATE TABLE e (a INT); -- empty\r\nSELECT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM t WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM e));\r\n-- expected true, got false\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Uncorrelated `EXISTS` is planned as `LIMIT 1`, then `COUNT(*)`, then `count == 1` (see `plan_subquery.cpp`).\r\n- Statistics propagate bottom-up",
      "parent_count": 1,
      "expected": "accept",
      "human_reason": "исправление с issue, правка src/ и test/sql",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "src/optimizer/statistics/operator/propagate_aggregate.cpp",
          "status": "modified",
          "additions": 5,
          "deletions": 0
        },
        {
          "path": "test/sql/subquery/exists/test_issue_26401.test",
          "status": "added",
          "additions": 40,
          "deletions": 0
        }
      ]
    },
