      "subject": "Preserve casts in list comprehension rewrites",
      "body": "Nested list lambdas can return an incorrect value when the list-comprehension rewrite discards casts: converting `[2]` through `INTEGER → BOOLEAN → INTEGER` currently returns `[2]` instead of `[1]`. Filter cast chains and struct cast chains can likewise change results; `TRY_CAST` can become a throwing cast. Fixes #26507.\n\nThe matcher currently unwraps arbitrary casts to recognize the parser's `filter`/`result` struct pattern, but the replacement does not recreate them. Restrict matching to direc",
