      "pr_number": 26057,
      "sha": "5d75ffff7bd0568b53c05aec1b9525bae9812212",
      "base_sha": "",
      "subject": "Fix FILL extrapolation for decreasing integer runs (#26042)",
      "body": "Fixes #26042\n\n## Problem\nFILL extrapolates incorrectly for the integer paths when the anchor values are in a *decreasing* run (lo > hi). The exchanged-frame slope was computed as -d, but by the affine identity\n\n    lo + d*(hi - lo) == hi + (1 - d)*(lo - hi)\n\nthe correct slope is 1 - d.\n\nRepro from the issue:\n    CREATE TABLE t(x BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, y BIGINT);\n    INSERT INTO t VALUES (1, 19), (2, 5), (3, NULL);\n    SELECT x, FILL(y) OVER (ORDER BY x) AS fill_y, FILL(-y) OVER (ORDER BY x) AS fill",
      "parent_count": 1,
      "expected": "accept",
      "human_reason": "исправление FILL с issue, правка src/ и test/sql",
      "files": [
