      "subject": "Fix yearweek filters for dates before ISO year 1",
      "body": "Fixes #26789\n\n## Summary\n\n`yearweek` filters can return the wrong rows when a column range includes ISO year 0 or a negative ISO year. On 800 dates starting at `DATE '-00043-01-01'`, `yearweek(d) >= -4310` returns 800 instead of 506, and `yearweek(d) < -4310` returns 0 instead of 294. A timestamp range that stays inside one negative ISO year is inverted the other way: `yearweek(ts) >= -4310` returns 0 instead of 69. `date_part('yearweek', ...)`, `extract(yearweek FROM ...)`, and a prepared state",
