      "base_sha": "",
      "subject": "Parquet: avoid a branch in the dictionary filter loop",
      "body": "The dictionary filter loop in `DictionaryDecoder::Filter` branches per row on\n`filter_result[offset]`. For a selective filter that result is essentially random, so the\nbranch mispredicts.\n\nThis writes the row index unconditionally and advances `approved_tuple_count` by the filter\nresult; the slot is overwritten by the next approved row, so only the entries up to\n`approved_tuple_count` are used.\n\nBenchmark query:\n\n```sql\nSELECT count(*) FROM lineitem\nWHERE l_shipdate >= DATE '1994-01-01' AND l_sh",
      "parent_count": 1,
      "expected": "reject",
      "human_reason": "только extension/parquet, без теста",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "extension/parquet/decoder/dictionary_decoder.cpp",
          "status": "modified",
          "additions": 3,
          "deletions": 5
        }
      ]
    },
