      "body": "`tpch_queries()`, `tpcds_queries()` and the `tpch()` / `tpcds()` pragmas take an optional scale factor, positionally or as `sf=...`:\n\n```sql\nSELECT * FROM tpch_queries(sf=100);\nSELECT * FROM tpcds_queries(10);\nPRAGMA tpch(11, sf=100);\nPRAGMA tpcds(9, sf=10);\n```\n\nThe returned queries carry the substitution parameters the official generators produce for that scale factor. Without a scale factor the stored queries are returned unchanged, byte for byte.\n\n### What depends on the scale factor\n\nChecke",
